. Networking Setup (VPC, Subnet, IGW)

This is the foundation for all AWS infrastructure.

    VPC: VPC Dashboard > Create VPC > VPC only > Name: my-vpc, CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16.

    Subnet: Subnets > Create > Select my-vpc > Name: public-sn, CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24.

    Internet Gateway: Internet Gateways > Create > my-igw.

        Action: Select my-igw > Attach to VPC > Select my-vpc.

    Routing: Route Tables > Select the table for my-vpc > Routes > Edit routes.

        Add Route: Destination 0.0.0.0/0, Target: Internet Gateway (my-igw).

    Association: Route Tables > Subnet associations > Edit > Select public-sn.

2. EC2 Instance Launch (Inside VPC)

    Step 1: EC2 Dashboard > Launch Instance.

    Step 2: Choose Ubuntu and t3.micro.

    Step 3: Under Network Settings > Edit:

        VPC: my-vpc

        Subnet: public-sn

        Auto-assign Public IP: Enable.

    Step 4: Security Group: Add SSH (22) from My IP and HTTP (80) from 0.0.0.0/0.

    Step 5: Select/Create Key Pair and click Launch.

3. S3 Storage Operations

    Create Bucket: S3 > Create bucket > Name: unique-name-123 > Create.

    Upload: Open bucket > Upload > Drag/Drop index.html.

    Public Access (If required):

        Permissions tab > Edit > Uncheck Block all public access > Save.

        Select file > Actions > Make public via ACL.

4. IAM Roles (EC2 to S3 Connection)

This allows your server to talk to storage without using hardcoded passwords.

    Create Role: IAM > Roles > Create role > AWS Service > EC2.

    Permissions: Search and check AmazonS3FullAccess.

    Name: EC2-S3-Role > Create.

    Attach: EC2 Dashboard > Select Instance > Actions > Security > Modify IAM Role.

    Test: In the EC2 terminal, run:
    Bash

    aws s3 ls

5. Bastion Host (Jump Server) Logic

To access a private instance that has no public IP:

    Bastion: Launch in public-sn with Public IP enabled.

    Private EC2: Launch in private-sn with Public IP disabled.

    Security Group (Private): Edit Inbound rules > SSH (22) > Source: Select the Security Group ID of the Bastion.

    Connect:

Bash

    # Copy key to Bastion
    scp -i key.pem key.pem ubuntu@bastion-ip:~/.
    # SSH into Bastion
    ssh -i key.pem ubuntu@bastion-ip
    # SSH from Bastion to Private
    ssh -i key.pem ubuntu@private-ip
    ```



